# Keep the build context minimal: node_modules/ alone would dwarf everything
# Dockerfile.test actually needs, and the whole context is packaged and sent to the
# daemon before the build starts. That cost is worse when the checkout sits on a
# network share, which is common for this project (see Dockerfile.test).
#
# Strategy: ignore everything, then re-include exactly what gets COPYed.
*

!requirements_test.txt
!pytest.ini
!custom_components/
!tests/

# ...but never ship Python caches. They can carry bytecode compiled by the Windows
# interpreter, which has no business inside a Linux image.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc

# tests/ holds the card's vitest suites too. The image runs pytest only, so they
# are context (and image layers) spent on files nothing in here will execute.
tests/card/
